# Private git worktrees of the hssd_blender_ir submodule. Several sessions
# edit that module at once, so each takes a sibling checkout rather than
# sharing one working tree. They carry their own .git and must never be
# swept into this repo by a `git add -A`; that is a worse 095a5be, not a
# fix for it. Trailing slash so only directories match.
#
# To check this rule, probe WITH a trailing slash:
#   git check-ignore -q modules/hssd_blender_ir_<name>/   -> 0, ignored
# Without it you are asking about a FILE of that name, which this rule does
# not cover, so a sibling that does not exist yet answers 1 and reads exactly
# like no rule at all.
modules/hssd_blender_ir_*/
